  "explanation": "Soil texture refers to the proportion of sand, silt, and clay particles and how they aggregate. Adding organic matter from the decomposition of plants and animals (humus) binds these particles into stable aggregates, improving aeration, water retention, and overall soil structure. This directly enhances soil texture. The other options—runoff, erosion, and compaction—either remove fine particles or compress the soil, which degrade rather than improve texture.",
